@startuml
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
skinparam noteTextAlignment left
' purpose: every byte proveo's vendored sbx kits differ from UpstreamKitsRef, and when each delta can go
' covers: internal/sbx/third_party/opencode.yaml
' covers: internal/sbx/upstream_test.go (TestVendoredKitJqFiltersCompile)
' see: _spec/internal/sbx/sbx-kit-v3.puml (UPSTREAM KITS)
'
' ── RULE ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
' third_party/ is a copy of docker/sbx-kits-contrib at UpstreamKitsRef. A local
' edit is a delta: it is listed here with its upstream report, and a re-vendor
' re-checks each one (drop it when upstream carries the fix, re-apply otherwise).
'
' ── DELTA 1: opencode import filter, one `}` (2026-10-28) ──────────────────
' MEASURED on Fedora, sbx 0.50.0, proveo dev@b6309a0, opencode + ChatGPT subscription:
'   `sbx secret ls`                    openai (oauth configured)
'   SBX_CRED_OPENAI_MODE               oauth
'   ~/.local/share/opencode/auth.json  access/refresh == oai-oat01/oai-ort01-proxy-managed
'   `opencode auth export`             []        ← no sbx-openai record
'   opencode                           request without the subscription's auth header
' The startup hook "Import sandbox OAuth credentials into OpenCode v2" reshapes
' auth.json into `opencode auth import` records with jq. Its `oauth()` def opens
' `then {` and closes only the `value: (…)` parens before `else empty end`:
'   jq: error: syntax error, unexpected else, expecting '}' … line 19
' The hook catches that as "auth.json is not valid OpenCode OAuth data" and exits 0,
' so every start imports nothing. jq 1.7 and 1.8.1 reject it alike (MEASURED).
' Present at 8b0844a and on sbx-kits-contrib main (f1979e6, 2026-10-26).
' Delta: `else {} end))` → `else {} end))}`. With it the filter yields
'   [{"id":"sbx-openai","integrationID":"openai","label":"Sandbox OpenAI","active":true,
'     "value":{"type":"oauth","methodID":"chatgpt-browser",…}}]
' TestVendoredKitJqFiltersCompile compiles every jq filter in every vendored
' lifecycle hook (jq -n, bound args null/""; exit 3 = compile error) and fails
' on this delta's absence.
' Upstream report: not yet filed (drafted for review 2026-10-28).
' Drop when: UpstreamKitsRef includes the brace.
title Vendored kit deltas

file "docker/sbx-kits-contrib\n@UpstreamKitsRef" as UP <<cloud>>
file "internal/sbx/third_party/opencode.yaml\n+ `}` (delta 1)" as VEN <<app>>
component "TestVendoredKitJqFiltersCompile\njq -n per hook filter" as T <<app>>
component "sandbox start\nImport sandbox OAuth → opencode auth import" as HOOK <<cloud>>

UP --> VEN : vendor + deltas
VEN --> T : every jq filter compiles
VEN --> HOOK : lifecycle@1 copied by UpstreamKitFor
@enduml
